    30	> - **Fragments and knowledge:** thirteen fragments; **deployment thirty-three** (coordinator ruling: the read at the seep on the 302nd stands and is counted). The thirteenth is Force-adjacent from Teague, partial Bronze, unused; it listens along a braced heel-to-palm line and costs back along that line. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know of it; **Oryn has NOT been told** (coordinator ruling: fix 25 declined — she refused the count at the fence on the 304th, and Cael means to tell her when she will hear it); Teague and Vastin do not. Teague is the second unpaid acquisition debt, beside Vastin. The twelfth has leaned outward at the west pier and at fourteen made sheets, never inward here. The two words *still/set* remain Cael's alone (`chapter-50.md:121–157`; `chapter-51.md:55–75,311–351`; `chapter-52.md:71–101`; `chapter-53.md:75–151`).
    31	> - **What went east:** seven hooded watch members left singly with a day's start. They saw Brom take two bolts on silent Iron, Teague move the barricade with silent Force, and five people—including a boy and an old man on a stick—stand and walk inside the line. They saw nothing work inside and nobody die. They carried the broken bow; the sound bow and one stave remained at the post (`chapter-50.md:35–65,99–105,181–301`; `chapter-51.md:7–11`).
    32	> - **Bodies:** the broad man's right shin is knit, boarded and stick-bearing; his crossbow stock is split. Teague's right wrist/elbow are in linen to the shoulder on a slat and the hand is unreliable; a third use would mean a splint. Brom has a breastbone bruise and ridged left-forearm bruise through a week of colours. Cael has a ten-day left collar-bone welt. Vastin's right knee is day twenty-six of thirty. Two men—Vastin and the broad man—are on sticks (`chapter-51.md:15–37,79–175`; `chapter-52.md:3–9`; `chapter-53.md:17–67,265`).
    33	> - **Teague's crew:** they know five people crossed and stood whole and that a boy did it with a stick; they do not know mechanism, fragments, leaf, lamps page, slips, date, Vastin's former office, or “behind it.” The young one follows where he is looked at; the tall man and older healer still have not spoken to the six (`chapter-50.md:181–299`; `chapter-51.md:79–175`).
    34	> - **Three record objects/pages:** (1) Karis holds the torn lamps-finding leaf in the back of her notebook, filed on its own; (2) Cael holds the folded fair copy of the chamber leaf in Hesk's book/coat, still not quoted; (3) the technician's sheet remains at the foot of the second row in the flat, its deep-layer date known separately to Cael and Seln and said/written by neither. No line joins (1) and (2), and Cael added no page of his own (`chapter-52.md:181–221`; `chapter-53.md:263–275`).
    35	> - **Map point and notch:** the fifth point is a thumbnail ring around the prick, uninked until corded. The bearing runs through the square notch; Seln looked from a mile, saw no fire, person, movement or heel-mark, disliked the absence, and will look again from nearer at first light before Teague moves (`chapter-52.md:149–157`; `chapter-53.md:233–261,281–289`).
    36	> - **Oryn:** five days past the noon-300 cairn; she stayed for Brom's week, Vastin's knee and the large edge, with three holds still owed and word already sent. She has not heard the chamber leaf. She does NOT yet know of the thirteenth or of what it would cost his ribs (coordinator ruling), and does not know *still/set* (`chapter-47.md:195–245`; `chapter-53.md:25,265`; fix 25).
    37	> - **Seln:** he has looked at the pass and said only “I looked at it.” His case remains shut on his chest, contents unnamed (`chapter-49.md:187–219`; `chapter-53.md:233–261`).
    38	> - **Day, bodies, money and load:** night of the 305th; twelve people and the brown mule; purse 123; no purse spend after the four marks. The mule bears three boxes, the flat, meal, Oryn's pannier and canvas. Karis has the hide/pinned sheet, brass, notebook, Cleon's roll, three-box sheet, Vastin's copied page and nine pier sheets; Cael has Hesk's book, shut dividers and folded fair copy; Vastin has the tarred kit case with cord, mallet and never-driven stake thirty-two. The two slips are re-pinned under the oldest row's knot, seals unnamed (`chapter-52.md:41–69,225–283`; `chapter-53.md:263–289`).
    39	
    40	> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 1]
    41	
