     3	Same author, same method (NO-SOURCE: do not open `books/` or `v3-runs/`). You may read this edition's own closed text and the plan. The four Sol reads are in this folder (`plan-audit.md`, `source-tracking.md`, `review-editorial.md`, `review-cold.md`); read their findings, and read `plan-audit-apply.md` for what the coordinator took and declined and why. Do NOT read the audit's section 5.2 ("Minimal restorations and protected-source notes") or its "Exact line fixes" list, and do not read the quoted source sentences in `source-tracking.md`'s table: they print the old text. The baseline is `pre-repair-r1/` (your draft plus the fourteen coordinator-applied fixes). Write `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md` when done and refresh AUTHOR-REPORT's "New canon minted" and "State at movement end".
     4	
     5	**Verdict on the draft:** ratified. The pass and its seven flights, the seated wall, the death and how it is handled, the first use of the thirteenth, the burial, both healers, the inward turn and the log handed back unread, the court and its arithmetic, the centre, the three cutaways, the ledger, the letter, the departures and the closing prose all stand. Nothing is to be re-staged. All twenty-five of your flags are answered KEEP except where B and C below say otherwise. This is the lightest repair of the book: joins round eleven restored units (six `{{JOIN}}` beats), two tracked passages in chapter 55, and four sentences. The movement stands at about 36,600 words; do not grow it.
