     7	## A. KEPT (ruled; not to change)
     8	
     9	1. **The wall, sitting** (Oryn's term amended by her, at his asking, seated, the leg laid out; it spends him). It mints one bounded thing — an Iron Wall can be raised through whatever its holder has set upon the ground — and later books will honour it.
    10	2. **The death** as you staged it: the hurt man's look; the hand that closes on air; the boots twenty strides behind; "Leave me!"; Oryn asking, waiting a breath, and going in without; the name said once and not rendered.
    11	3. **Force on the second stack's brace**, along the shelf, at nobody, with the ribs paying; Teague on the stair, untold, reading "the look of a bill" and not asking.
    12	4. **Deployment thirty-five** (thirty-three; the brace, thirty-four; the twelfth turned on the court's floor on purpose, thirty-five; the inward self-reading uncounted, as the five with the tenth were).
    13	5. Oryn told of the thirteenth at the ribs; "No term tonight" and its reason; the instruments by lamp; Lira pushing the book back; the court's form (cut, eleven stumps, courses, peg-holes, the word from Ostrand); the round corded and the sum; the copied slip of the tool; both edges; "No sixth found."; the council's fourth sentence; the marks going south; the walk and the count; "He fit." / "It was not an accident." / the step left lying; Vastin's night ("since he was fourteen" stands: it is when any sigil comes and states no age); Oryn riding north to the salt road (closed chapter 49 has the road); Vastin the sixth by Seln's count; your paragraph before the closing prose; "said Cael" after "I'll tell you on the road,".
    14	
    15	## B. Already applied by the coordinator (keep the protected words exactly; write the joins)
    16	
    17	`{{JOIN}}` marks a place where a beat of YOURS belongs. Six are on the page; none may remain. Attributions outside the quotation marks are the coordinator's, flat on purpose: vary, move or drop them. The words inside the quotation marks are fixed.
    18	
    19	1. **ch54:** `"It's through," Cael said.` — the speaker is CAEL, over his own drawing, when the three ways have been priced. It is the boy with the book who says where the line goes, to a captain whose field it is; Teague's "Then here's what I see in it" answers him. Re-join the paragraph before (his thought of the wall across a road) into it.
    20	2. **ch55, the last line:** `It was not ink.` — narration, Cael's understanding on the lip above the plain, with the blanket being set down behind him. Only "was not ink" is fixed; the sentence as it stands is the minimal form. You may give it one sentence of lead-in if the turn from "a thing made with a pencil" wants it, but it should stay the chapter's last line and stay short. Do not explain it.
    21	3. **ch57:** `The same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's.` — narration, whole, his one summing. Check the sentence before and after still meet it.
    22	4. **ch58:** `"The others are copies," said Karis.`
    23	5. **ch58, at the cut:** Vastin — `"I stood at a line for forty years," Vastin said, "and told people which side of it they were. I never once asked who drew it."` `{{JOIN}}` `"This is where they drew it."` Both his; the join is his look, or the breath, before the second. Your paragraph after it (the stick over, the stiff leg, back) stands.
    24	6. **ch58:** Oryn — `"Nothing," Oryn said. "Everything, round it."` `{{JOIN}}` `"Same as you."` The third is said with her eyes on Cael, as you staged it; it goes unanswered.
    25	7. **ch58:** Teague — `"My crew's stood at four of these. It's stood at enough," Teague said.` `{{JOIN}}` `"Field's mine. This isn't field."` The second is said to Cael (he gave him the ground past the iron at the Span with "Say how."; this is the same ruling in his own words).
    26	8. **ch58, the close:** now on the page — Lira: "Every other one, yours worked and ours died." / Cael: "Yes." / Lira: "You think this one's different." / Cael's two-part speech / "He stepped over the line." / "His Path did not die. It also did not *notice* it should have." / `"Wait here," he said, and did not look back, and walked toward the center of the oldest quiet, alone.` The narration lines are protected as printed (OWNER #57; "center" as printed). Trim the attributions to what a listener needs; nothing is added after the last line.
    27	9. **ch59:** `"Twenty-nine tomorrow," Vastin said.` / `"Thirty's the month," said Oryn.` — your paragraph after it ("the only other count that anybody had left that night") stands.
    28	10. **ch60, Teague's going:** `"The thaw's past," Teague said.` / `"Noted," said Cael.` / `"After the next thaw."` `{{JOIN}}` `"Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes."` — all but the "Noted" are Teague's. This is the first time that Cael's word is given to this man at a parting; the join is small.
    29	11. **ch60, Oryn's going:** `"The day I have to," Oryn said.` / `"Noted," said Cael.` / `"Everybody says that."` `{{JOIN}}` `"They'll carry. They'll hurt," Oryn said.` `{{JOIN}}` `"After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say."` — your question about the leaf stands before it. At the Span she said "Everybody says that now,"; this is its echo, a little shorter.
    30	12. **Small things done:** "a brass rule read false by two hairs" (no instrument is given an intent); "walked all this way to say" for "walked a year" (the plan allows a year only in the log and the closing prose); Oryn now says of Karis's palm, "It'll leave a line," (the plan's body ledger quotes it; check that the sentences round it sit well, and move it within that paragraph if it reads better elsewhere).
