    29	*Owed, in money: nothing. Owed otherwise, and entered side by side: to Vastin, the eleventh, which came while he held a wall for us in a stair. To Teague, the thirteenth, which came at a stride while I kept his left. Neither has been told. Neither can be until the whole of it can be, and the whole of it is six people's. I used the second of them yesterday over that captain's head, on a thing that would have killed him. It does not pay the debt. A debt is not paid by something that the creditor is not let to know.*
