    49	"Then I shall add one thing to it, which you may enter or not. Those people have reached for us three times. They came up a stair under a town, and they stood to a pair of timbers at a fence, and yesterday they let a hill go." His voice was as mild as ever. "Each time they have gone away again, and each time they knew a little more than they had known. I have never once seen what any of them looks like. I do not think that the third was the last."
