+### Coordinator's specific questions
+
+a. **KEEP** Karis's new line at 60:191, `I have a use for lines.` It is a concise, character-specific answer to Oryn, recalls Karis's work without asserting a new fact, and gives the scar beat a clean human turn. It does not trespass on any protected unit.
+
+b. **Both tagless lines are unmistakable by ear.** `Right.` follows `Lira brought the boot back` (58:273–277). `It's the first one.` follows `Karis went over ... She stood` (58:289–293). Each speaker is named in the immediately preceding sentence, and neither surrounding character can plausibly own the line.
+
+c. **All three joins are original to this edition, not imported stage directions.** Source 23:85 has `He looked at the floor.`; the repair instead has Vastin lift his eyes and follow the cut left and right (58:309). Source 23:91 has `She looked at Cael.`; the repair distinguishes what Oryn says to the floor from what she turns to say to him (58:327). Source 23:97 has `He looked at Cael.`; the repair has Teague look round at the boy in the missing shoulder-place (58:349). The gloss at 58:353 is supported by closed chapter 50:181–183, `Say how.` / `By count,` and adds no event or knowledge.
+
+d. **The win is legible without a summing sentence.** A thirteen-year-old can follow who did what and what bought the time: the wall receives the fall and shuts the mouth; the cleared bank becomes a climb; Seln is found above; the broad man and Brom draw the bows; Force moves the second rig; Teague takes the stair; the nine leave. `Nine.` closes the opposition count, while the dust roof and brown coat show the price (55:65–89, 175–315). The causal chain is dramatized rather than recapitulated.
+
+e. **The length cuts remove no plan fact or binding ledger bullet.** The stumps remain eleven and their locations are counted; the ruled court geometry does not require the deleted observation that they are unevenly set. The ledger still rules that using the thirteenth does not pay Teague's debt, so the deleted deliberation duplicates rather than carries that fact (60:29). Karis still declines to append to Hesk's letter and says she would rather carry her own paper (60:73–79). No exit-state fact is lost.
+
+f. **The chapter-57 cord speech is whole.** The repaired line is one continuous quotation: `I'm taking one more reading for it. Tomorrow you'll put that cord ...` (57:107). The coordinator's join removes the false stop between two parts of the same speech without changing sense or speaker.
+
+g. **The Vastin sentence is true and properly narrow.** `He had asked for no place among them ... and nobody had offered him one` (60:281) coexists with his specific earlier requests without contradicting them. The later reminder that he once asked for a bed (60:291) reinforces the distinction. Nothing hints that he requested or was invited to come.
